From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: asus-zenbook-a16-snapdragon-x2-elite-linux <30148248+hasanaktas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Camera stack for Glymur and the ASUS Zenbook A16 (OV02C10 RGB,
 HM1092 IR) on linux-omarchy 7.3-78

The FixItFoundry/zenbook-a16-linux stable camera series, rebased onto
linux-omarchy 7.3-78 as one diff. The individual patches, with their
original authors and trailers, are in upstream-camera/:

  0026  camera subset of the 0028 snapshot: glymur CAMSS, the standalone
        MIPI CSI2 PHY driver and CCI changes (its cci_resume_runtime()
        hunk dropped: linux-omarchy already resets the controller there)
  0027  regulator: qcom-rpmh: add PMH0104 camera LDOs
  0100  arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Add CAMSS and CSIPHY nodes (Nihal Kumar Gupta)
  0101  arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Add CCI definitions
  0102  arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Add camera MCLK pinctrl
  0103  i2c: cci: require exact clock rates
  0104  mfd: pm8010 over I2C
  0105  regulator: pm8010
  0106  media: i2c: add HM1092 (Ramshouriesh R)
  0107  camss: limit Glymur to the validated nonsecure capture path
  0108  arm64: dts: wire the A16 RGB and IR cameras
  0109  i2c: cci: clock stretching
  0133  clk: qcom: Fix camera rivian PLL configuration settings
  0155  A16: drive the RGB camera MCLK at 6 mA (Jesse Casco)
  0156  media: i2c: hm1092: wire up .set_fmt on the sensor pad (Jesse Casco)
  0157  A16: wire the PMH0101 IR emitter (Jesse Casco)
  0159  camss: x1e80100: use the lite clocks
  0160  camss: x1e80100: fix CSID2 routing
  0161  camss: use the full X1E80100 tables for Glymur

Source: https://github.com/FixItFoundry/zenbook-a16-linux (patches/stable)
Needs CONFIG_VIDEO_HM1092=m and CONFIG_PHY_QCOM_MIPI_CSI2=m.
